<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:59:02Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Zambia's opposition criticizes government restructuring and layoffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:598b5cfe94c726892306ac39e4a2396281d2f0f6c2faffc99f2898df85c1161e</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:59:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/zambia-s-opposition-criticizes-government-restructuring-and-layoffs/a-79875892--f6feaaea394e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zambia-s-opposition-criticizes-government-restructuring-and-layoffs/a-79875892?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Government-backed dismissals and restructuring are fueling debate in Zambia. Opposition politicians are questioning the transparency of the plans; officials say the changes are necessary.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tanzania: Opposition leader Tundu Lissu jailed for four years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3955e74147ee2f3ec3210c973f924711f6b6eef1ee89937dd5473666c592d99</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:57:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tanzania-opposition-leader-tundu-lissu-jailed-for-four-years/a-79875248--8689ad1af62d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tanzania-opposition-leader-tundu-lissu-jailed-for-four-years/a-79875248?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tanzanian opposition leader Tundu Lissu has been sentenced to four years in prison after being cleared of treason. Lissu condemned his conviction for incitement, which had not been among the charges he faced.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya cult leader Paul Mackenzie sentenced to 200 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15441bfdb9cceacac19b03886839c3a952e751c37bc2f3cb30db3605c302c49b</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:57:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-cult-leader-paul-mackenzie-sentenced-to-200-years/a-79875112--7a13b520397b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-cult-leader-paul-mackenzie-sentenced-to-200-years/a-79875112?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A court in Kenya has sentenced Paul Mackenzie to 200 years in prison for the murders of 190 children and an adult. He told them to starve themselves to death as part of his apocalyptic religious cult.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wawira Njiru, Kenya's school feeder and German Africa Prize recipient</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38b244c1fe6603721cea95e20eab1058f07c888abb070023ed2435ccca160d98</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:57:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wawira-njiru-kenya-s-school-feeder-and-german-africa-prize-recipient/a-79646537--47b719bb31e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wawira-njiru-kenya-s-school-feeder-and-german-africa-prize-recipient/a-79646537?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Standing ovations in Berlin: Kenyan social entrepreneur Wawira Njiru received the German Africa Award for her school feeding programme, which now provides meals to 730,000 children every day.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will renewed conflict derail Ethiopia's economic growth?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a102b677a2e73eff4237197713f83d563ac813a66d55aafcdb1dbe82aa63160a</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:57:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T11:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-renewed-conflict-derail-ethiopia-s-economic-growth/a-79807060--aec9783cc542.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-renewed-conflict-derail-ethiopia-s-economic-growth/a-79807060?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia's economy is growing strongly. But renewed fighting in the north of the BRICS member state could deter investment, strain public finances and push up the cost of living.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
